WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
In Cambodia stands Angkor Wat.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.990
It was built in the early
1100s for the Hindu god Vishnu.

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.100
That is a long way from India,
where Hindu traditions began.

4
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.900
An old Hindu text says the soul
puts off a body like worn-out robes,

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.370
and takes a new one.

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:22.070
So how did ideas about the soul,
duty and devotion shape lives,

7
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.700
and even kingdoms?

8
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.140
In this mission, you'll follow
the soul's cycle of birth,

9
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.120
death and rebirth, and learn what dharma,

10
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.510
a person's duty, asks.

11
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.080
Then you'll visit Hindu kingdoms from
South India to Cambodia and Java,

12
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.280
and ask what held them together.

13
00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: find out how Hindu ideas shaped
both everyday lives and great kingdoms.
